{"id": "2d6a64d4-ec6c-40dc-b6a6-186f42809e73", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a bounded configuration review rather than open-ended root-cause work — I need to check the endpoint setup, async inference config, autoscaling policies, and CloudWatch metrics. Given the symptom described (silent drops, queue backup), delegating to a subagent seems token-inefficient since it'd require multiple API calls.

I'll proceed without asking, tell the user my plan, then call a subagent named sagemaker-async-review, preloading relevant skills like exploring-metrics and searching-logs. I'll default to region us-east-1 and account 123456789012 unless told otherwise, and craft a structured prompt for the subagent.

"}]}

{"id": "2b04e2b2-ce6d-4c0c-806c-4293ac160d28", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review your SageMaker async inference setup. That means the endpoint and endpoint config, the async output and failure paths, the autoscaling policies, and the recent queue and error metrics. Then I'll report which settings could cause silent drops or queue buildup.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_rSxMH7aFdNlcy2tjdLpEA6", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-async-posture-review", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review the configuration posture of the SageMaker asynchronous inference endpoint(s) serving the LLM and identify misconfigurations that could explain (a) requests being silently dropped and (b) the queue backing up.",
  "context": "User reports their SageMaker async inference endpoint for an LLM seems to drop requests silently and the queue sometimes backs up. They want a posture/config review of what is misconfigured, not a full root-cause hunt. Agent space is in account 123456789012, region us-east-1 (check other associated accounts/regions via list_associations if no async endpoint is found there). Use read-only operations only. First discover async endpoints (list_endpoints, describe_endpoint, describe_endpoint_config; an endpoint is async if its config has AsyncInferenceConfig). If multiple exist, prioritize the one that looks like an LLM (name, model, large GPU instance types, inference components) and mention the others briefly.",
  "resources": ["SageMaker endpoints and endpoint configs in us-east-1 account 123456789012", "Application Auto Scaling scalable targets/policies for the endpoint variant", "SNS topics referenced in AsyncInferenceConfig.OutputConfig.NotificationConfig", "S3 output/failure paths and KMS key", "Model/container config and CloudWatch log group /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints/<name>"],
  "timeframe": "Last 24 hours for metrics, ending 2026-11-17T19:00:00Z (extend to 7 days for trend if useful)",
  "criteria": "Check and report on: (1) AsyncInferenceConfig: ClientConfig.MaxConcurrentInvocationsPerInstance (vs. what the LLM container can really handle), OutputConfig S3OutputPath / S3FailurePath set, SNS SuccessTopic and ErrorTopic configured (missing ErrorTopic/FailurePath = silent failures), and whether those SNS topics exist, have subscriptions, and permissive/encrypted properly; S3 bucket/KMS access for the execution role (use read-only checks only, do not modify). (2) Autoscaling: is there a scalable target, min capacity (scale-to-zero or min=0 with no HasBacklogWithoutCapacity step policy?), max capacity, the metric used (ApproximateBacklogSizePerInstance vs. invocations-per-instance), target value, cooldowns (scale-out too slow for LLM model load times), instance quota limits. (3) Container/model: InvocationTimeoutSeconds (ModelClientConfig) vs. LLM latency, container startup health check timeout, instance type/volume size, payload size vs. 1 GB async limit, inference-request retention (async requests expire after 6 hours in queue). (4) Metrics: ApproximateBacklogSize, ApproximateBacklogSizePerInstance, ApproximateAgeOfOldestRequest, HasBacklogWithoutCapacity, RequestsFailed/ RequestsSucceeded-type async metrics (InvocationsProcessed, InvocationFailures, InvocationModelErrors, Invocation4XXErrors/5XXErrors), TimeInBacklog, ProcessingTime, CPU/GPU/Memory utilization, instance count over time. (5) Logs: scan the endpoint log group for OOM, timeouts, CUDA errors, container restarts or 'model not loaded' errors. Return a concise prioritized list of misconfigurations/risks with evidence (resource names, values, timestamps), severity, and the suggested fix for each, plus what you could not verify. Do not make any changes."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review SageMaker async endpoint config, autoscaling, and queue metrics"}], "created_at": null}

